{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass.</b> One wonders about the arranger of the sections why he joined this verse to those that follow it, for it is attached to them. And if we do not know the reason for it — for thus [it says] 'on the day YHWH spoke to Moses in the land of Egypt' — and this is that He spoke to him: 'I am YHWH; speak to Pharaoh.' And like it: 'And it came to pass, when all the men of war were finished dying from among the people' (Deuteronomy 2:16), which is joined to the section adjacent to it. Perhaps the one who made the divisions knows a reason why he did so, for his knowledge is broader than our knowledge."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:15.239051239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}